        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="1">
                    <English>Unknown</English>
                    <French>Inconnu</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>During the infiltration test we notice air leakage through the followings house component:

- Windows: Kitchen, Master bedroom

- Door: Left door (dining room), balcony door, and probably also the main entrance door.

- Receptacles

- Dryer



The result is not very high, but with the replacment of the weather strips of the doors and the windows it would be possible to increase the air tightness.</airSeal>
                <ceilingsCathedral>Unfortunately the access to the roof was not possible. Therefore the level of insulation of the attic is an estimation of similar houses builted in the same year.</ceilingsCathedral>
                <HeatingSystem>The owner mention the idea of adding a secondary heating system. We suggest the installation of an Air source heat pump. This type of equipment can be 3 times more efficient than a simple baseboard. We recommend to consult a specialist to see if this type of equipment is good for your home. Remember that this type of heating system require a secondary heating sytem to ensure the heating when the outdoor temperature are to low.</HeatingSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
